       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose is well above the labeled maximum for metformin.\n\n- **Ordered:** 1700 mg three times daily, which is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Labeled maximum:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release in adults. The usual maximum single dose is 850 mg to 1,000 mg. Extended-release is capped at 2,000 mg/day to 2,550 mg/day, taken once daily or in divided doses.\n- **Risk:** At this dose, even with normal kidney and liver function, the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 1,700 mg total daily, divided as 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- Another regimen, such as extended-release\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is what you want, tell me and I'll enter it with a note that the dose was confirmed as intended. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
